A||||5||84_duke||removing interior panels - seatbelt in the way!?||||5||
Z||000000||84_duke||12-11-2001||12:32 PM||||I am trying to get the panels off that have the seatbelt in them, but cant figure out how to get the top seatbelt bolt unscrewed.<BR>anyone?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Standard||12-11-2001||12:37 PM||||You need a T50 Torx bit.  There's a little plastic cover over the bolt, pops up from one end if it hasn't already broken.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||12-11-2001||12:38 PM||||You need to get a T50 Torx bit - lift the plastic cover and do your thing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||12-11-2001||12:39 PM||||Pop the tan or grey cover from the side.  Underneath is a bolt that takes a #50 torx socket.<P>LOL, this place is great!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 12-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||84_duke||12-11-2001||12:54 PM||||hey guys thanks a lot... if that is the same size as the bolt on the bottom... i just used a really big alan key and some muscle to get it off... we'll see!<P>------------------<BR>84_duke||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||12-11-2001||02:41 PM||||I just use a large allen key myself. If its too tite to break loose, just use vise grips to get it broken loose. cover hides it anyway if it gets scratched.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 12-11-2001).]||||reg||1
